        '''Insert blank character'' button: inserts a non-breaking space (NBSP) into the Name field (it is not treated as a blank space). 
If placed at the beginning of a shortcut''s name, the shortcut will be moved to the special character category at the top of your Start Menu list (folder names cannot retain NBSP characters).',
        'Not every symbol renders the same in Start; the simulation reflects what your chosen font/Start rendering will likely show after apply.',
        '**It is possible that certain emojis and characters could cause rendering problems in the actual Start Menu, in which case removing that character will resolve the issue.'
      )
    },
    [pscustomobject]@{
      Title = 'Profiles Tab'
      Items = @(
        'Profiles - displays profile-specific context for folders and shortcuts.',
        'Use ''Simulated Start Menu (default selection)'' for a simulated view of your current operating system''s Start Menu layout.'
